# tiberius: the AVX-512 expert tier without VBMI, against upstream 5e8a4cca (v0.2.7, engine 0.1.52).
#
# THE PROBLEM.  cpu_avx512_ok() is the one gate the AVX-512 expert kernels were selected through, and it
# demanded AVX512-VBMI.  This box's CPU (Cascade Lake) has F/DQ/BW/VL/VNNI and BMI2 but no VBMI, so the VNNI
# kernels sat behind a gate that excluded it, and there was no honest way to relax the gate: it also selects
# the trellis AVX-512 kernel (tq_cpu.cpp; tq_avx512.cpp is compiled with -mavx512vbmi and documents
# F/BW/VL/VBMI/VNNI).  Dropping VBMI from the shared gate would admit a VBMI-less CPU to that TU: SIGILL in the
# middle of a token, exactly the failure class the startup probe exists to prevent.  So the gate is SPLIT:
#
#   cpu_avx512_ok()       F/DQ/BW/VL + VNNI + VBMI   the full gate; trellis (tq_avx512.cpp) stays behind it.
#   cpu_avx512_vnni_ok()  F/DQ/BW/VL + VNNI        new; every VBMI-free kernel: expert.cpp, iq_avx512.cpp,
#                                                    nvfp4_avx512.cpp, dsv41's iq512x rows (no VBMI in these
#                                                    TUs with the flag removed).
#
# Both use the same OSXSAVE/XCR0 probe, STRATA_FORCE_AVX2 handling and STRATA_FORCE_ISA cap.  The new gate is
# stricter in one dimension (DQ) because its TUs are compiled with -mavx512dq.
#
# WHAT ELSE CHANGED, and why:
#   * expert.cpp: the two VPMULTISHIFTQB unpacks are replaced by VPERMW + VPSRLVW + VPMOVWB + VINSERTI*,
#     expanding the SAME fixed shift pattern (byte i = (u16 >> 2i) & 3).  Byte-identical to the old layout.
#     This is what lets expert.cpp drop -mavx512vbmi.
#   * CMakeLists.txt and sycl/CMakeLists.txt: -mavx512vbmi removed from expert.cpp and from the iq_avx512.cpp
#     + nvfp4_avx512.cpp flag lists; KEPT on tq_avx512.cpp (the trellis TU).  Upstream 0.2.7 compiles the
#     iq/nvfp4 TUs with -mavx512vpopcntdq -mbmi2 as well; both stay, and the gate is NOT widened for them:
#     its feature list remains F/DQ/BW/VL/VNNI (BMI2 is untested on purpose - every AVX-512 VNNI part has it,
#     and the executed rows do not need it).  VPOPCNTDQ is not in the gate either: the only vpopcnt use in the
#     TU is sign_mask_from_idx, which is reached only from iq512x_rows - itself gated by iq512x_supported(),
#     which tests VPOPCNTDQ at run time.  Measured on this box (no VPOPCNTDQ): ~50 requests, including 26-28k
#     prompts that walk the whole AVX-512 expert tier, with zero SIGILL and zero Xid.
#   * Call sites routed to the new gate: expert_layout.cpp's q2_rows_any / q2_rows_any_legacy / act_quant_any;
#     native_expert.cpp's avx512, cpu512, nvfp4_512 (2x), exact_one and iq3s_one guards;
#     nvfp4_avx512_parity.cpp (2x); native_expert_parity.cpp; iq_avx2_parity.cpp and kq_cpu_bench.cpp banners;
#     and generate.cpp's "this CPU has no AVX-512" expert-kernel log line.  dsv41/ds4_gg_cpu.cpp follows.
#   * Left on cpu_avx512_ok(): tq_cpu.cpp / tq_cpu_parity.cpp (trellis, compiled with VBMI) and dsv41's
#     ds4_iq_cpu.cpp / ds4_gguf_cpu.cpp (their own VBMI/build checks).
#   * The MSVC /arch:AVX512 branches are unchanged.
#
# Measured on tiberius 2026-10-18 (ab18 campaign, 3 counterbalanced runs per arm): ~5% cheaper CPU expert
# pool+plan per decode window, GPU wait and Optane reads unchanged, outputs numerically sound (parity 0
# failures vs the ggml references) but NOT bit-identical to the AVX-2 tier on the long cells.
# See docs/exec-plans/active/tiberius-kernel-tuning.md.
